description:
Path: crate-jmap-server/src/backend.rs:89-93. `pub fn with_description(mut self, desc: impl Into<String>) -> Self` — docstring is one line:
  /// Set the human-readable description.

The JmapBackend::Error security contract added in commit 8099de3 (backend.rs:618-645) is a long, detailed MUST-NOT list:
  - Credential material (auth tokens, push verification codes, etc.)
  - Blob content (email bodies, sieve scripts, etc.)
  - PII shaped like an email address

That contract is on the trait's associated Error type because Error::Display is the value that flows through handle_get/handle_changes/handle_query/handle_query_changes → JmapError::server_fail(e.to_string()) → wire.

SetError.description has the EXACT same threat surface but no warning:
- It is serialized into wire-format SetError objects in /set responses (RFC 8620 §5.3 `notCreated`/`notUpdated`/`notDestroyed` maps).
- A handler/backend implementor writing `SetError::new(t).with_description(format!("{e}"))` where `e` is a backend error, an internal exception, or any downstream service's error, recreates the same leak class.
- It is in fact MORE leak-prone than serverFail.description, because SetError fires for every invalid input — adversarial clients can probe for SetError descriptions by sending crafted /set arguments.

The reference *-server crates emit SetError descriptions in many places. crate-jmap-mail-server/src/submission.rs has 3 SetError construction sites (rg confirms: SetErrorType::InvalidRecipients, NoRecipients, CannotUnsend). Each constructs a typed SetError, none currently leaks — but the API gives no signal that future contributors need to think about this.

Right shape: add a parallel "Security" docstring section to SetError::with_description:

  /// # Security
  ///
  /// `SetError.description` is serialized verbatim into the JMAP wire
  /// response (RFC 8620 §5.3) and is visible to any client that can
  /// dispatch the failing /set call. The same MUST-NOT rules that apply
  /// to `JmapBackend::Error::Display` (credential material, blob content,
  /// PII shaped like an email address) apply to this string. Wrap
  /// downstream errors with `JmapError::server_fail` (which has its own
  /// description handling) rather than interpolating them here.

This is a 10-line doc-only change; no API surface change, no test change. The cost of leaving it as-is is: a future contributor doing the natural-looking `with_description(format!("{e}"))` ships a leak class on a /set path with no review tripwire because the doc comment is silent.

Pair this finding with JMAP-wlip.2 (the parallel serverFail.description leak path). The Display contract on the backend trait is necessary; the matching warning on SetError::with_description is also necessary.
